IMPORT prelude

-- Control of Vectors and Pesticides Act 1998 (Singapore) -- registration of pesticides and vector repellents (s 5), creating
-- conditions favourable to vectors and its presumption (s 15), permission to breed or keep vectors (s 16), clearing vegetation near
-- water (s 19), who must be registered, licensed or certified to do vector control work (ss 24-27), how long a registration, licence
-- or certificate lasts (s 30), appeal periods and whether a decision bites while an appeal is pending (ss 12, 13, 17, 32), entry
-- into a dwelling-house (s 35(3)), the maximum penalties (ss 14, 23, 34, 37, 38, 45, 48), liability of officers of a body
-- corporate (s 49) and the time limit for a complaint (s 50).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CVPA1998.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/7/2026"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 15 of 2026
-- (wef 01/07/2026), to the definition of "owner" in s 2.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties, offences, thresholds and
-- deadlines an ordinary householder, business, pesticide seller or pest-control firm meets. Not encoded: the application and
-- registration procedure for pesticides (ss 6-9) beyond s 5, cancellation grounds (ss 10, 31) as such, sampling and detention
-- powers (s 13) beyond the appeal period, the Director-General's orders and self-help powers (ss 17, 18, 20-22, 36) beyond the
-- appeal period and penalty, costs recovery (ss 39-44), arrest and court procedure (ss 46, 47, 51, 52), composition (s 53),
-- evidence (s 58), exemptions (s 59) and regulations (s 60). The meaning of "vector" (s 2) is taken as a given fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Control of Vectors and Pesticides Act 1998 -- control`

§§ `5 -- pesticides and vector repellents must be registered`

-- s 5(1): a person must not (a) "advertise any pesticide as being suitable for the purpose of vector control"; (b) "sell or supply
-- any pesticide for the purpose of vector control"; or (c) "advertise, sell or supply any substance, mixture or preparation as being
-- suitable for repelling vectors", unless it is registered under s 7.
-- s 5(2): a registered pesticide or vector repellent must not be SOLD "otherwise than in a container or package" bearing a label
-- "that the Director-General has approved" showing the prescribed particulars.
-- s 5(3): a vector control operator, technician or worker "must not use any pesticide for the purpose of carrying out any vector
-- control work unless the pesticide is registered".
--
-- s 5(2) speaks only of selling. "Supply" is defined separately in s 2 ("includes having in possession for the purpose of supply").
-- Reading s 5(2) as not reaching a supply that is not a sale is an inference from the words used. s 5 says nothing about a private
-- person using a pesticide at home.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `advertising a pesticide for vector control`
    `selling a pesticide for vector control`
    `supplying a pesticide for vector control without selling it`
    `selling a vector repellent`
    `a vector control technician using a pesticide in vector control work`
    `a householder using a pesticide at home`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs a registered product` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `a householder using a pesticide at home` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a sale` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `selling a pesticide for vector control` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling a vector repellent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `the product is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the label is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity contravenes section 5` IF
        (`the activity needs a registered product` `the activity` AND (NOT `the product is registered`))
    OR  (`the activity is a sale` `the activity` AND (NOT `the label is approved`))

§§ `15 -- conditions favourable to vectors, and the presumption against the owner or occupier`

-- s 15(1): "A person must not create, or cause or permit to be created, any condition favourable to the propagation or harbouring
-- of vectors."
-- s 15(4): if "it is shown that the condition on any premises, vessel or aircraft is favourable to the propagation or harbouring of
-- vectors, it is presumed, unless the contrary is proved, that the condition is created, or caused or permitted to be created, by
-- the owner or occupier".
GIVEN `a favourable condition is shown on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused is the owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accused proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is presumed to have created the condition` IF
    `a favourable condition is shown on the premises` AND `the accused is the owner or occupier` AND (NOT `the accused proved the contrary`)

§§ `16 -- breeding, keeping or importing vectors`

-- s 16(1): no one may "breed, keep, collect, distribute, sell, import or export any vectors without the written permission of the
-- Director-General". (3): the Director-General "may refuse the application without giving any reason". (4): the Director-General
-- "must not grant permission" unless satisfied the application is for (a) "a scientific purpose"; (b) "purposes of education or
-- research"; or (c) "any other purpose that is acceptable to the Director-General". (6): revocable at any time without reason.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `a scientific purpose`
    `education`
    `research`
    `some other purpose`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the Director-General finds the purpose acceptable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permission to breed vectors may be granted` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `some other purpose` THEN `the Director-General finds the purpose acceptable`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `19 -- clearing undergrowth near water`

-- s 19: where on any land there is "any stream or seepage or running or standing water to which shade may be afforded by the
-- development of undergrowth or other vegetation", a person must not cut down or clear "any undergrowth or vegetation within 6
-- metres" of it "without the prior approval of the Director-General".
-- Reading exactly 6 metres as "within 6 metres" is an inference.
GIVEN `the water could be shaded by vegetation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the distance from the water in metres` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Director-General approved beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clearing contravenes section 19` IF
        `the water could be shaded by vegetation`
    AND `the distance from the water in metres` AT MOST 6
    AND (NOT `the Director-General approved beforehand`)

§§ `24 to 27 -- who may do vector control work`

-- s 24: a person must not, "in the course of any trade or business, undertake or engage in vector control work", or hold itself out
-- as a vector control operator, "unless the person is registered as a vector control operator".
-- s 25: no one may act as a vector control technician "unless he or she is licensed or provisionally licensed".
-- s 26: no one may act as a vector control worker "unless he or she is certified or provisionally certified".
-- s 27: a registered operator must not employ or engage anyone to do technician's or worker's work unless so licensed or certified.
-- s 2: a "vector control technician" "for reward or under a contract of employment, carries out or supervises" vector control work;
-- a "vector control worker" carries it out "under the supervision of a vector control technician".
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a pest-control business`
    `a technician`
    `a worker`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `holds a full authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a provisional authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may do the work` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a pest-control business` THEN `holds a full authorisation`
    OTHERWISE `holds a full authorisation` OR `holds a provisional authorisation`

GIVEN `the employee is licensed or certified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employee is provisionally licensed or certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator contravenes section 27` IF
    (NOT `the employee is licensed or certified`) AND (NOT `the employee is provisionally licensed or certified`)

§§ `30 -- how long it lasts`

-- s 30(1): the registration of an operator, a technician's licence and a worker's certificate are "each valid for a period of 3
-- years from the date of the grant". (2): a provisional licence or certificate "is each valid for a period of 9 months". All may
-- be renewed.
DECLARE Authorisation IS ONE OF
    `an operator's registration`
    `a technician's licence`
    `a worker's certificate`
    `a provisional technician's licence`
    `a provisional worker's certificate`

GIVEN `the authorisation` IS AN Authorisation
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the validity in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the authorisation`
    WHEN `a provisional technician's licence` THEN 9
    WHEN `a provisional worker's certificate` THEN 9
    OTHERWISE 36

§§ `12, 13, 17 and 32 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 12(1): conditions on, or cancellation of, a pesticide registration -- appeal "within 14 days of the date of receiving the
-- notice"; (2): a condition or cancellation "takes effect from the date specified by the Director-General, unless the Minister
-- otherwise directs".
-- s 13(3): seizure or detention of a consignment -- appeal "within 14 days of the action". (6): the consignment is released when
-- analysis clears it or "the Minister on an appeal ... so directs". That detention continues meanwhile is read from (6).
-- s 17(9): an order to take measures against vectors -- appeal "within 3 days of the order"; (10): the order "takes effect from the
-- date stated in the order, unless the Minister otherwise directs".
-- s 32(1): conditions, refusal, suspension or cancellation of an operator's registration, licence or certificate -- 14 days of
-- receiving the notice; (2): a condition takes effect unless the Minister otherwise orders; but (3): where notice of appeal is duly
-- given, "the suspension or cancellation ... does not take effect unless it is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is for any
-- reason dismissed".
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a condition on a pesticide registration`
    `cancellation of a pesticide registration`
    `seizure of a pesticide consignment`
    `an order to take measures against vectors`
    `a condition on a pest-control authorisation`
    `suspension or cancellation of a pest-control authorisation`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appeal period in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `an order to take measures against vectors` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 14

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `the Minister has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision bites while a timely appeal is pending` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `suspension or cancellation of a pest-control authorisation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `the Minister has directed otherwise`

§§ `35(3) -- entering a home`

-- s 35(1): the Director-General or an authorised officer may enter any premises, vessel or aircraft. (3): "A person must not,
-- except with the consent of the occupier thereof, enter any dwelling-house by virtue of the powers conferred by this section
-- without at least 12 hours' previous notice being given to the occupier".
GIVEN `the premises is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is allowed` IF
        (NOT `the premises is a dwelling-house`)
    OR  `the occupier consented`
    OR  `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 12

§§ `14, 23, 34, 37, 38, 45, 48 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 14 (Part 3, pesticides): "$20,000 or ... 3 months or ... both"; second or subsequent conviction "$50,000 or ... 6 months".
-- s 23 (Part 4, vectors): (a) "in the case of an offence under section 17" -- the same $20,000 / 3 months, then $50,000 / 6 months;
-- (b) "in any other case" -- $5,000 / 3 months, then $10,000 / 6 months.
-- s 34 (Part 5, operators): $20,000 / 3 months, then $50,000 / 6 months.
-- s 37(2)(a) (using premises so as to damage anti-breeding works): "a fine not exceeding $10,000". s 38(1) (damaging works executed
-- by order): "a fine not exceeding $10,000". Neither provides imprisonment or a higher repeat penalty.
-- s 45 (obstruction): $5,000 or 3 months. s 48(3) (refusing or misstating name and address): $1,000.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `selling an unregistered pesticide`
    `failing to comply with a section 17 order`
    `creating conditions favourable to vectors`
    `breeding vectors without permission`
    `clearing vegetation near water without approval`
    `running an unregistered pest-control business`
    `using premises so as to damage anti-breeding works`
    `damaging works done by order`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `misstating a name or address`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence carries the higher Part penalty` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `selling an unregistered pesticide` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `failing to comply with a section 17 order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `running an unregistered pest-control business` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence carries the lower Part 4 penalty` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `creating conditions favourable to vectors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breeding vectors without permission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `clearing vegetation near water without approval` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence carries the higher Part penalty` `the offence`
    THEN `the higher Part fine` `a second or subsequent conviction`
    ELSE IF `the offence carries the lower Part 4 penalty` `the offence`
         THEN `the lower Part 4 fine` `a second or subsequent conviction`
         ELSE `the fixed fine` `the offence`

GIVEN `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher Part fine` MEANS
    IF `repeat` THEN 50000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower Part 4 fine` MEANS
    IF `repeat` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using premises so as to damage anti-breeding works` THEN 10000
    WHEN `damaging works done by order` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 1000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `a second or subsequent conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offence carries the higher Part penalty` `the offence` OR `the offence carries the lower Part 4 penalty` `the offence`
    THEN `the Part imprisonment` `a second or subsequent conviction`
    ELSE `the fixed imprisonment` `the offence`

GIVEN `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `repeat` THEN 6 ELSE 3

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `49 -- officers of a body corporate`

-- s 49: where a body corporate, partnership or unincorporated association commits an offence, a director, manager, partner,
-- secretary or similar officer "shall be guilty of that offence unless he or she proves that" (a) it was committed "without his or
-- her consent or connivance"; AND (b) he or she "had exercised all such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he
-- or she ought to have exercised".
GIVEN `the body committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person was an officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty too` IF
        `the body committed an offence`
    AND `the person was an officer at the time`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

§§ `50 -- time limit for a complaint`

-- s 50: "Except in any case where, by reason of the act or omission complained of, any injury or danger to health subsists at the
-- date of the complaint", no one is liable unless the complaint "is made within 12 months after the date of the commission of the
-- offence".
GIVEN `months from the offence to the complaint` IS A NUMBER, `danger to health still subsists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the complaint is in time` IF
    `danger to health still subsists` OR `months from the offence to the complaint` AT MOST 12
